 "design": "R6 the coverage figure the main-text limitation rests on, at five times the replicates.\n\nDesign fixed before running (2026-09-16, written 12:45 EDT). The manuscript's largest disclosed weakness\nis stated as a number. A run effect that follows the size band rather than the recipe takes coverage of\nthe recipe-clustered interval to 0.810 when it holds a quarter of latent variance and to 0.579 at a half,\nand both figures appear in the main text. They came from 2,000 replicates, which puts the Monte Carlo\nstandard error near 0.009 on the first and near 0.011 on the second. A reader deciding how seriously to\ntake a limitation should not have to wonder whether 0.810 is really 0.82, so this run repeats the zero,\nquarter and half cells at 10,000 replicates with a fresh seed, which brings the standard error to about\n0.004. The generator, the four interval constructions and the shipped-estimator check are unchanged, so\nthe two runs compare directly and pool if they agree. The three-quarter cell is dropped, because 0.348 is\nfar enough from nominal that its precision changes nothing a reader would decide differently.\nSeed 20260952 and a cell offset of three thousand keep the draws distinct from the first pass.\n",
